IMPORT prelude

-- Road Vehicles (Special Powers) Act 1960 (Singapore) -- the whole Act: definitions (s 2), the duty to stop and the power to search
-- (s 3), seizure and forfeiture of vehicles (s 4), the duty to identify the driver (s 5), penalties (s 6), and the Schedule of
-- scheduled offences.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (all amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/RVSPA1960.txt, marked "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 14/4/2026". The latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 5 of 2026 wef 14/04/2026 (s 4(8) and s 7).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0094 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (seven sections and a Schedule), so this row takes all of it. Not encoded: s 1 (short title),
-- s 7 (the Minister may amend the Schedule by Gazette order), the content of the Public Order and Safety (Special Powers) Act 2018
-- (a "special authorisation" is an input here), and the elements of each scheduled offence (an offence is named by its provision).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Vehicles (Special Powers) Act 1960`

§§ `2 and the Schedule -- scheduled offences`

-- s 2: "scheduled offence" means any offence specified in the Schedule.
-- Schedule para 1: offences punishable under (a) Arms Offences Act s 3(1), (2); (b), (c) listed sections of the repealed Betting
-- and Common Gaming Houses Acts; (d) Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act ss 3 to 6; (e) Hostage-Taking Act
-- s 3; (f) Miscellaneous Offences (Public Order and Nuisance) Act s 27(2), (3); (g) Misuse of Drugs Act "sections 5, 6, 7, 8(a),
-- 11F(1), 11G(1), 11H(1) and 11I(1)(a)"; (h) Internal Security Act s 59; (i) Societies Act s 14(3); (j) Penal Code "sections 143,
-- 144, 145, 147, 148, 302, 307, 324, 325, 326, 363, 363A, 364, 364A (as in force before 21 November 2010), 365, 368, 506, and
-- Chapter 17"; (ja) listed sections of the Gambling Control Act 2022; (k) Penal Code s 120B "where the criminal conspiracy is to
-- commit any of the offences set out in the foregoing sub-paragraphs".
-- Para 2: "Attempts to commit and abetment of any of the offences set out in paragraph 1."
--
-- Misuse of Drugs Act s 8(a) is possession; s 8(b), consumption, is not listed (read in the deposited Misuse of Drugs Act). Penal
-- Code Chapter 17 is "Offences against property" (theft, s 379, among them -- read in the deposited Penal Code). Penal Code s 279
-- (rash driving) and Road Traffic Act offences are not listed.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `Arms Offences Act s 3(1)`
    `Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act s 6`
    `Hostage-Taking Act s 3`
    `Misuse of Drugs Act s 5 (trafficking)`
    `Misuse of Drugs Act s 8(a) (possession)`
    `Misuse of Drugs Act s 8(b) (consumption)`
    `Internal Security Act s 59`
    `Societies Act s 14(3)`
    `Penal Code s 147 (rioting)`
    `Penal Code s 302 (murder)`
    `Penal Code s 363 (kidnapping)`
    `Penal Code s 506 (criminal intimidation)`
    `Penal Code s 379 (theft, in Chapter 17)`
    `Penal Code s 279 (rash driving)`
    `Gambling Control Act 2022 s 19(2)`
    `a Road Traffic Act offence`

DECLARE Involvement IS ONE OF
    `committing it`
    `attempting it`
    `abetting it`
    `conspiring to commit it`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is listed in paragraph 1` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `Misuse of Drugs Act s 8(b) (consumption)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Penal Code s 279 (rash driving)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Road Traffic Act offence` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Para 1(k) and para 2: a conspiracy, an attempt or an abetment is scheduled exactly when the offence aimed at is in para 1.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the involvement` IS AN Involvement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a scheduled offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the involvement`
    WHEN `committing it` THEN `the offence is listed in paragraph 1` `the offence`
    WHEN `attempting it` THEN `the offence is listed in paragraph 1` `the offence`
    WHEN `abetting it` THEN `the offence is listed in paragraph 1` `the offence`
    WHEN `conspiring to commit it` THEN `the offence is listed in paragraph 1` `the offence`

-- s 2: "road" means "any public road or any other road, to which the public has access, and includes bridges over which a road
-- passes".
GIVEN `is a public road` IS A BOOLEAN, `the public has access` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a road` IF
    `is a public road` OR `the public has access`

§§ `3 -- the duty to stop and the power to search`

-- s 3(1): the person driving or in control of any road vehicle "in motion must stop the vehicle on being required to do so by any
-- police officer in uniform". s 6(1): contravention is an offence.
GIVEN `the vehicle is in motion` IS A BOOLEAN, `required to stop by a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the officer is in uniform` IS A BOOLEAN, `stopped` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to stop is an offence` IF
    `the vehicle is in motion` AND `required to stop by a police officer` AND `the officer is in uniform` AND (NOT `stopped`)

-- s 3(2): (a) "as respects any road vehicle being on any road"; or (b) "upon the overtaking of a road vehicle" whose driver was
-- required to stop under (1) "but has failed to do so" -- any police officer may search the vehicle and any person found in it IF
-- the officer "suspects on reasonable grounds" that an article in respect of which a scheduled offence has been or is being
-- committed is in the vehicle, or that the vehicle, or a person in, on or near it, is the target of a special authorisation under
-- the Public Order and Safety (Special Powers) Act 2018, or that the vehicle is in an area that is the target of one.
-- Limb (b) does not require a road: a vehicle chased off the road after failing to stop may still be searched.
GIVEN `on a road` IS A BOOLEAN, `overtaken after failing to stop` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably suspects a scheduled-offence article` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably suspects a special-authorisation target` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a police officer may search the vehicle and its occupants` IF
        (`on a road` OR `overtaken after failing to stop`)
    AND (`reasonably suspects a scheduled-offence article` OR `reasonably suspects a special-authorisation target`)

§§ `4 -- seizure and forfeiture`

-- s 4(1), (6): the three uses that make a vehicle liable -- (a) "in the commission of a scheduled offence or that any scheduled
-- offence has been committed in respect of the road vehicle or in respect of any article found in the road vehicle or on any person
-- found in the road vehicle"; (b) "to convey persons to the scene where a scheduled offence has been committed"; (c) "for the
-- escape or to facilitate the escape of any person from the scene of a scheduled offence". s 5(1) uses the same list.
DECLARE VehicleUse IS ONE OF
    `used in committing a scheduled offence`
    `a scheduled offence committed in respect of it or an article in it`
    `conveying persons to the scene of a scheduled offence`
    `an escape from the scene of a scheduled offence`
    `parked near the scene but not used`
    `used in an offence that is not scheduled`

GIVEN `the use` IS A VehicleUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use makes the vehicle liable to forfeiture` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `parked near the scene but not used` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `used in an offence that is not scheduled` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 4(8) (Act 5 of 2026): "Despite subsections (1) and (6), a court need not make an order for the forfeiture" if it is proved that
-- the person who committed the scheduled offence "(a) is not the owner of the road vehicle; and (b) had used the road vehicle without
-- the consent of the owner".
GIVEN `proved the offender is not the owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved the use was without the owner's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-consenting owner exception is made out` IF
    `proved the offender is not the owner` AND `proved the use was without the owner's consent`

-- s 4(1): where the use is proved and "the road vehicle has been seized by the police, the court is, on the written application of
-- the Attorney-General, to make an order for the forfeiture of the road vehicle, notwithstanding that no person may have been
-- convicted of any scheduled offence". Read with s 4(8), which turns "is to" into "need not".
GIVEN `the use` IS A VehicleUse, `seized by the police` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Attorney-General applied in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `someone was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the offender is not the owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved the use was without the owner's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must order forfeiture` IF
        `the use makes the vehicle liable to forfeiture` `the use`
    AND `seized by the police`
    AND `the Attorney-General applied in writing`
    AND (NOT `the non-consenting owner exception is made out` `proved the offender is not the owner` `proved the use was without the owner's consent`)

-- s 4(4): "If there be no prosecution with regard to any scheduled offence, the road vehicle seized under subsection (2) must be
-- forfeited at the expiry of one month from the date of seizure unless a claim to the road vehicle is made before that date." A
-- claim is written notice to the Commissioner of Police by a person asserting ownership, "personally or by that person's agent
-- authorised in writing".
DECLARE Claimant IS ONE OF
    `the person asserting ownership, personally`
    `an agent authorised in writing`
    `an agent authorised orally`
    `a family member with no written authority`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant, `notice in writing to the Commissioner of Police` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid claim is made` IF
        `notice in writing to the Commissioner of Police`
    AND CONSIDER `the claimant`
        WHEN `the person asserting ownership, personally` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an agent authorised in writing` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(8) speaks only of a court order, so it does not reach the forfeiture that happens of itself under s 4(4).
GIVEN `there was a prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN, `one month from seizure has expired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a valid claim was made within the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle is forfeited without any order` IF
    (NOT `there was a prosecution`) AND `one month from seizure has expired` AND (NOT `a valid claim was made within the month`)

-- s 4(5): on a claim the Commissioner "may direct that the road vehicle be released or may refer the matter by information to a
-- Magistrate". s 4(6): the Magistrate "is to hold an inquiry" and on proof of a liable use "is to order the road vehicle to be
-- forfeited or may in the absence of such proof order its release". s 4(8) applies "despite subsections (1) and (6)".
GIVEN `the use is proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `the use` IS A VehicleUse,
      `proved the offender is not the owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved the use was without the owner's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Magistrate must order forfeiture` IF
        `the use is proved`
    AND `the use makes the vehicle liable to forfeiture` `the use`
    AND (NOT `the non-consenting owner exception is made out` `proved the offender is not the owner` `proved the use was without the owner's consent`)

-- s 4(7): in proceedings about a seizure, a person is not entitled "to the costs of the proceedings or to any damages or other relief
-- other than an order for the return of the road vehicle, unless such seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause".
DECLARE Relief IS ONE OF
    `return of the vehicle`
    `costs of the proceedings`
    `damages`
    `other relief`

GIVEN `the relief` IS A Relief, `seized without reasonable or probable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relief is open to the claimant` IF
    CONSIDER `the relief`
    WHEN `return of the vehicle` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `seized without reasonable or probable cause`

§§ `5 -- the duty to identify the driver`

-- s 5(1) (a vehicle alleged or suspected of a liable use) and s 5(2) (a special authorisation in effect and a reasonable suspicion
-- of a target, or of a dangerous article, offensive weapon or subversive document): (a) "the owner of the road vehicle must give any
-- information ... as to the identity and the address, driving licence number and identity card number of the person who was in
-- control of or driving the road vehicle on any specified occasion"; (b) "any other person who was or should have been in control of
-- that road vehicle must ... give any information which is in that person's power to give and which may lead to the identification
-- of the driver".
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the owner`
    `the driver at the time`
    `a person who should have been in control`
    `a passenger`
    `a bystander`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must give information when required` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the owner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the driver at the time` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person who should have been in control` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 5(3): no contravention if the person satisfies the court "(a) that the person did not know and could not with reasonable
-- diligence have ascertained the information required; or (b) that owing to circumstances over which the person had no control, it
-- was impossible for the person to give, before the date on which the person was charged with such contravention, the information".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `required by a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave the information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `could not have known with reasonable diligence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `impossible before being charged, for reasons beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to give information is an offence` IF
        `the person must give information when required` `the person`
    AND `required by a police officer`
    AND (NOT `gave the information`)
    AND (NOT `could not have known with reasonable diligence`)
    AND (NOT `impossible before being charged, for reasons beyond control`)

-- s 5(4): "Notwithstanding anything in any other written law, any information given under this section by any person charged with
-- any offence under this Act or with any scheduled offence may be used in evidence at the hearing of the charge."
GIVEN `given under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN, `the informant is charged under this Act or with a scheduled offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information may be used in evidence against the informant` IF
    `given under section 5` AND `the informant is charged under this Act or with a scheduled offence`

§§ `6 -- penalties`

-- s 6(1): contravening the Act "(except section 5(2))": "a fine not exceeding $1,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6
-- months or to both". s 6(2): contravening s 5(2): "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years
-- or to both".
DECLARE Contravention IS ONE OF
    `failing to stop under s 3(1)`
    `withholding particulars under s 5(1)`
    `withholding particulars under s 5(2)`

GIVEN `the contravention` IS A Contravention
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine in dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `the contravention`
    WHEN `withholding particulars under s 5(2)` THEN 20000
    OTHERWISE 1000

GIVEN `the contravention` IS A Contravention
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the contravention`
    WHEN `withholding particulars under s 5(2)` THEN 24
    OTHERWISE 6
